<title>USA: U.S. administration electric bill in early stages.</title>
<headline>U.S. administration electric bill in early stages.</headline>
<byline>Sonali Paul</byline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Clinton administration is weighing whether to call for new utility pollution limits in legislation it is drafting to spur power market competition nationwide, administration officials said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Details of the bill have yet to be approved within the Energy Department, which is leading the effort, but a department official said it could be ready for review by other agencies &quot;maybe within the next month.&quot; (c) Reuters Limited 1997</p>
</text>
